<title>SPAIN: BBV sees 20 pct full-year profit rise.</title>
<headline>BBV sees 20 pct full-year profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Bilbao Vizcaya expects to end the year with a rise in net attributable profit of 20 percent, given continued positive developments in trading and in net interest income, a top bank official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;At the end of the year the results (after minorities) will rise by about 20 percent,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The attributable profit for the group in the first nine months rose 26.5 percent to 70.5 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
